§ `Fourth Schedule Part 1 -- what the text says besides the table`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:7790 | Document fees must be paid at the time of filing or sealing (as the case may be) of the following specified documents with the electronic filing service provider or at any such time or manner the Registrar of the Supreme Court or State Courts (as the case may be) may determine: Items
@ref Sch 4 part 1 (src:7790)
GIVEN `the fee is a document fee for a document specified in Part 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee is paid at the time of filing or sealing (as the case may be) with the electronic filing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee is paid at the time or in the manner the Registrar of the Supreme Court or State Courts (as the case may be) has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 1 the document fee is paid as the Schedule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the fee is a document fee for a document specified in Part 1`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Document fees must be paid ... of the following specified documents"
    ELSE IF `the fee is paid at the time of filing or sealing (as the case may be) with the electronic filing service provider` OR `the fee is paid at the time or in the manner the Registrar of the Supreme Court or State Courts (as the case may be) has determined`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be paid"; the Schedule does not say what follows

-- Item 9: "$50 for each day that a document remains unfiled", "excluding non-court days, if imposed by the Court".
-- src:7955 | 9.
-- src:7956 | On late filing of a document that remains unfiled after the expiry of the period within which the document is required to be filed, excluding non‑court days, if imposed by the Court
-- src:7957 | $50 for each day that a document remains unfiled
-- src:7958 | $50 for each day that a document remains unfiled
-- src:7959 | $50 for each day that a document remains unfiled
-- src:7960 | $50 for each day that a document remains unfiled
-- src:7961 | The filed copy
@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 9 (src:7955-7961)
GIVEN `the last day` IS A DATE
      `the day the document is filed` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4 part 1 item 9 the number of court days the document remained unfiled` MEANS
    IF `the last day` AT LEAST `the day the document is filed`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (IF `o 1 r 3(1) a day is a non-court day` (`the last day` PLUS 1) calendar EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS `sch 4 part 1 item 9 the number of court days the document remained unfiled` (`the last day` PLUS 1) `the day the document is filed` calendar

@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 9 (src:7955-7961)
GIVEN `the Court imposes the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the period within which the document is required to be filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the document is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee is payable` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Court imposes the fee`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if imposed by the Court"
    ELSE IF `the date the document is filed` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period within which the document is required to be filed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the fee is for a document "that remains unfiled after the expiry of the period within which the document is required to be filed"

@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 9 (src:7955-7961)
GIVEN column IS A `sch 4 column`
      `the number of court days the document remained unfiled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 1 item 9 the late filing fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee in the row for the column` `sch 4 part 1 item 9 row` column
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column
    WHEN JUST fee THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee `the number of court days the document remained unfiled` 0 0 0

-- Item 43: "such fee (not exceeding the amount which would have been payable under item 40 if the bill had been allowed in full) as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum fee".
-- src:8322 | 43.
-- src:8323 | On the withdrawal of a bill of costs which has been filed for assessment of costs, such fee (not exceeding the amount which would have been payable under item 40 if the bill had been allowed in full) as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum fee of:
-- src:8324 | $200
-- src:8325 | $200
-- src:8326 | $100
-- src:8327 | $50
-- src:8328 | Bill of Costs
@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 43 (src:8322-8328)
GIVEN column IS A `sch 4 column`
      fee IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that would have been payable under item 40 if the bill had been allowed in full` IS A NUMBER
      `the fee appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is one the Schedule allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee in the row for the column` `sch 4 part 1 item 43 row` column
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column
    WHEN JUST minimumFee THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the least sum under the fee` minimumFee
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the minimum is not stated as a sum
        WHEN JUST least THEN
            IF fee GREATER THAN `the amount that would have been payable under item 40 if the bill had been allowed in full`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not exceeding the amount which would have been payable under item 40 if the bill had been allowed in full"
            ELSE IF fee LESS THAN least
                 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to a minimum fee of"
                 ELSE IF `the fee appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable"

-- Item 43's amount: the text states no sum, only that the fee is "such fee ... as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable", not below a minimum.
-- So `sch 4 the fee for this document` answers NOTHING for item 43 (it never turns the minimum into the fee), and the question a person can ask is whether the fee reaches the minimum.
-- src:8322 | 43.
-- src:8323 | On the withdrawal of a bill of costs which has been filed for assessment of costs, such fee (not exceeding the amount which would have been payable under item 40 if the bill had been allowed in full) as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum fee of:
-- src:8324 | $200
-- src:8325 | $200
-- src:8326 | $100
-- src:8327 | $50
-- src:8328 | Bill of Costs
@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 43 (src:8322-8328)
GIVEN column IS A `sch 4 column`
      fee IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 1 item 43 the fee is at least the minimum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee in the row for the column` `sch 4 part 1 item 43 row` column
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column
    WHEN JUST minimumFee THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the least sum under the fee` minimumFee
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the minimum is not stated as a sum
        WHEN JUST least THEN
            IF fee AT LEAST least
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to a minimum fee of" ($200 in the Supreme Court columns, $100 in the District Court column, $50 in the Magistrate's Court column)

-- Item 14's note: "An urgent order to attend court and/or to produce documents is an order that is issued less than 3 days before the trial of an action".
-- Item 13 is for such an order "other than an urgent order", so this question decides which of the two items an order falls under.
-- src:8034 | Note : An urgent order to attend court and/or to produce documents is an order that is issued less than 3 days before the trial of an action
@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 14 note (src:8034)
GIVEN `the date the order is issued` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the trial of the action` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 1 item 14 the order is an urgent order` MEANS
    IF `the date the order is issued` AT MOST `the first day of the trial of the action` AND `the date the order is issued` PLUS 3 GREATER THAN `the first day of the trial of the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is an order that is issued less than 3 days before the trial of an action"

-- Item 17: "On sealing or issuing any document, not being a judgment or order, where no other fee is prescribed by this Schedule.  Provided that this fee is not payable on an Order for Review of Detention".
