         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no electronic service charge is to be imposed for documents filed in applications under sections 12, 18 and 25 of the Legal Profession Act 1966"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Item 49(2): "where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, it is deemed to comprise 2 pages".
-- src:8405 | (2)
-- src:8406 | Provided that where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, it is deemed to comprise 2 pages
@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) (src:8405-8406)
GIVEN `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the document is deemed to comprise 2 pages` MEANS
    IF `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the document is remotely composed"

@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) (src:8405-8406)
GIVEN `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of pages the document has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the number of pages charged for` MEANS
    IF `sch 4 part 1 item 49(2) the document is deemed to comprise 2 pages` `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN 2
    ELSE `the number of pages the document has`

-- Items 51 to 53: which of the two columns the claim's date picks.
-- src:8416 | Note: For items 51, 52 and 53
-- src:8417 | ( a )
-- src:8418 | the fees under the heading “Magistrate’s Court” apply in relation to claims lodged under the Small Claims Tribunals Act before 1 November 2019
-- src:8419 | ( b )
-- src:8420 | the fees under the heading “District Court” apply in relation to claims lodged under the Small Claims Tribunals Act on or after 1 November 2019
@ref Sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 (src:8416-8420)
`sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 the date from which the District Court column applies` MEANS Date 1 11 2019

@ref Sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 (src:8416-8420)
GIVEN `the date the claim was lodged under the Small Claims Tribunals Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `sch 4 column`
`sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 the column that applies` MEANS
    IF `the date the claim was lodged under the Small Claims Tribunals Act` LESS THAN `sch 4 part 1 items 51 to 53 the date from which the District Court column applies`
    THEN `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court`
    ELSE `sch 4 column District Court`
